  "description": "KEYPUC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C208 H264 N16 O64 Sm4 Zn8. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 10 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn7 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn8 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.474-3.531 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.64-104.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm4Zn8L8(OAc)8](OH)4 (crystallographic formula C208H267N16O68Zn8Sm4). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
